    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter tonight\u2019s slate with **Pete Crow-Armstrong** serving as our clear focal point for production. With an elite efficiency score of 80.98, **Crow-Armstrong** benefits from a high-upside matchup against Ober. The combination of an elevated SP_xERA (4.80) and a significant 4% boost from Ober\u2019s slow delivery makes **Crow-Armstrong** our primary engine for stolen bases, the scarcest commodity in our current build. Alongside him, **Christian Yelich** (74.22) and **Kazuma Okamoto** (69.87) are mandatory starts; **Yelich** draws a massive 13% platoon edge against S. Alcantara, while **Okamoto** is primed to capitalize on Kay\u2019s subpar 4.67 xERA, bolstered by a strong spot in the three-hole.\n\nRegarding our tactical decisions, **Lars Nootbaar** and **Nelson Velazquez** provide high-floor utility against Merrill Kelly, who remains our most targeted opposing arm with a 5.29 xERA. While the lineup remains pending for several slots, we are closely monitoring the status of **Dillon Dingler** and **Colt Keith** against the left-handed Reid Detmers. **Keith** in particular remains a marginal start (43.57) due to the L/L disadvantage; he only maintains his spot because our bench options like **Casey Schmitt** (42.62) failed to clear the efficiency threshold required to displace him. **Schmitt** was the closest to cracking the starting nine, but his poor matchup against Bryce Miller\u2019s 2.85 xERA ultimately relegated him to the bench. \n\nRisks are concentrated on our catchers and infielders facing Detmers. **Dillon Dingler** is currently riding a favorable lineup spot, but his projection is suppressed by a 9% penalty due to Detmers' ability to suppress run environments. We are also wary of **Yordan Alvarez**; despite an elite 0.475 xwOBA, his score of 56.16 reflects the difficulty of facing Dean Kremer. We will continue to evaluate the final confirmed lineups, keeping **Trea Turner**, **Kyle Schwarber**, and **Hyeseong Kim** in reserve as we navigate this high-variance set of matchups.",
